  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "I got inspired to create this app after a watching an excellent video
    by Scott Manley on Youtube about Two Line Element Sets that describe satellites
    in orbit and the overflow of the NORAD IDs used to track them after the launch
    of Saramago in March of 2026. <link=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RpdgYoF_uqs\"><u>Watch
    it here!</u></link>\n\nDATASETS USED:\nOrbital GP Elements: <link=\"celestrak.org\"><u>CelesTrak</u></link>\nSatellite
    Information and Statistics (up to 2023): \n<link=\"https://www.ucs.org/resources/satellite-database\"><u>Union
    of Concerned Scientists Satellite Database</u></link>\nLaunch Site Locations:
    <link=\"https://www.wikipedia.org/resources/satellite-database\"><u>Wikipedia</u></link>\nSGP4
    Algorithm: Hoots, F. R., & Roehrich, R. L. (1980). Spacetrack Report No. 3: Models
    for propagation of NORAD element sets. Aerospace Defense Command, U.S. Air Force.\n\nAI
    DISCLAIMER:\nGenerative AI was used for debugging purposes as well as to implement
    certain functions such as converting between coordinate systems and managing
    app settings that are secondary to the function of the app and have been implemented
    many times outside of this app. No code or graphics that are central to the app's
    function (the SGP4 implementation, the Earth shader, etc.) were created by a
    Generative AI model. \n "
